From 81664154b2719e49706dda384a14b4f7de3e8434 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:29:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sync): preserve loop early-exit telemetry labels [daveey]

The loop service was suspended inside an iteration generator. Closing that
iterator in the caller's finally injected GeneratorExit, so intentional
SchemaAhead give-up looked like an error and actual failures lost their type.
CPU partitions and completion counts were correct; label-only assertions
were missing from the original early-close test.

Own the active service through an ExitStack in the caller's lexical context.
Normal iteration completion closes it before checking keep_running again;
early return exits cleanly, and real exceptions reach the service unchanged.
Resource cleanup remains outside the measured scope.

Deterministic real-loop regression: SchemaAhead return, RuntimeError and
KeyboardInterrupt all failed on original source, then passed after the fix.
Each asserts one record per partition and exact 2 local / 3 Board / 5 total
CPU units, plus identity-preserving propagation. Added zero/two-iteration
count and predicate boundary checks. Initial targeted suite 42 passed;
scripts/check --base origin/main: 21 checks passed. Full consumer run is
tracked by t_425b16143964c2be. No live CPU P1 or threshold changes.
